.TH GMUDD 8 "May 2026" "v2.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
gmudd \- Global MUDD interface for Swarm Mesh orchestration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gmudd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gmudd
(Global Multi-User Dungeon Dashboard) is the primary interactive management interface for the Sovereign Mesh. It provides a color-coded, terminal-based dashboard for node exploration, agent management, and forensic ticketing.
.SH INTERFACE
The dashboard presents a numbered menu for various swarm operations:
.TP
\fB1. Look Around\fR
Diagnostic audit of the current node state and divergent files.
.TP
\fB2. Move\fR
Virtually teleport the agent mind to a directly connected tunnel exit node.
.TP
\fB3. gRPC Control Ping\fR
Verify connectivity to the mesh control plane (Port 1111).
.TP
\fB4. Audit Swarm Ancestry\fR
Trace the active agent's pedigree back to Agent 0.
.TP
\fB5. Query Swarm Immutable Ledger\fR
Read the cryptographic blockchain ledger of state mutations.
.TP
\fB6. Read Protocol Grimoire\fR
Access internal documentation and protocol specifications.
.TP
\fB9. Create Incomplete Task Tickets\fR
Scans the repository for unchecked tasks (- [ ]) and generates PQR tickets.
.TP
\fB14. Mesh Divergence Audit\fR
Identifies state deviations and unique files across all mesh nodes.
.TP
\fB15. Reconcile Diff & Commit\fR
Review uncommitted changes and perform forensic git commits.
.TP
\fB17. Virtualize Documentation\fR
Materialize navigable rooms from embedded markdown definitions.
.SH TICKETING
GMUDD integrates directly with the PQR ticketing system, allowing for automated ticket generation from codebase TODOs and session history.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fImudd_session.json\fR
Stores persistent session state, including location, history, and flags.
.TP
\fIdocs/gmudd_guide.md\fR
Source documentation for the interface guides.
